; Tutorial_2_Install_and_Launch.inix -- installing DbDo and opening it.

[about]
Title=2 - Install and Launch
Intro=The installer, the boxes on its last page -- the screen reader scripts, the player, the model for its AI commands -- and DbDo opening from anywhere.
Setup=DbDo_setup.exe is downloaded from the DbDo page on GitHub.
Homework=Run the setup again; every box should now say Update or Reinstall.

[step]

Say=One want: DbDo on this computer, with what it works best with, in one sitting.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=I open the downloaded setup program and allow it to make changes.
Key=Enter
Hear=Setup - DbDo dialog
Hear=Welcome to the DbDo Setup Wizard
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The ordinary installer: Enter takes Next, and the defaults are right.
Key=Enter
Hear=Select Destination Location
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The last page offers what DbDo works best with, each as a box whose first word is the machine's state read for you: Install, Update or Reinstall.
Key=Tab
Hear=(the box for your screen reader's scripts, its first word, checked)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Scripts for the screen reader you use; the mpv player, which plays a record's stream; and, for the AI commands, Ollama and a model, downloaded once.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Install mpv check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: clearing a box you need. Space clears it; Space again ticks it back.
Key=Space
Hear=not checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Space.
Key=Space
Hear=checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter installs what is ticked.
Key=Enter
Hear=Finish button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Then the key that opens DbDo from anywhere.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Installed and open. If something was left out, run the setup again and tick its box; what is already current costs nothing.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Help is four keys away, the same in every Homer program. F1 opens the full documentation in the browser.
Key=F1
Hear=DbDo documentation
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus F1 opens the ReadMe, the short start, for when the full guide is more than you need today.
Key=Alt+Shift+F1
Hear=DbDo ReadMe
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus F1, About, says the version, so you always know which DbDo is installed.
Key=Alt+F1
Hear=About DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape, and F11 asks GitHub whether a newer version is out. If one is, Yes is the default, and Enter installs it.
Key=F11
Hear=Checking for a newer version
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The templates to practise on open with Alt plus Shift plus D, D for Database, from anywhere in DbDo. Each is a complete example: JobTrail for job hunting, BookTrail for reading, RadioTrail for stations to play.
Key=Alt+Shift+D
Hear=Template Databases dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the dialog. Once a database is open, Alt plus Backslash opens its folder in File Explorer, where its scripts and reports live beside it.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo ready
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Two more ways to learn the keys before you need them. Control plus F1 turns on the Key Describer: each key then says what it does instead of doing it.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer on
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now Control plus O only describes itself.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Open Database, Control plus O
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F1 again turns the describer off. Alt plus Shift plus H, Hotkey Summary, lists every key in a window you can search.
Key=Alt+Shift+H
Hear=Hotkey Summary
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes it, and the database is as it was.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo ready
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the answer.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What a box's first word tells you.
Key=
Hear=Install, Update or Reinstall

[step]

Say=The key that opens DbDo.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Control plus D
